WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.035
-We don't always
have enough time to cover

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:05.005
all of the recent news,
so here with a recap

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:06.672
is one of our writers,
Amber Ruffin,

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:08.908
in a segment we call
"Amber Says What."

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:10.676
♪♪

00:00:10.676 --> 00:00:13.612
-You guys,
things have been crazy.

00:00:13.612 --> 00:00:16.082
Okay, first of all, I found out

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:19.351
we weren't coming in to work
anymore, and I was like, "What?"

00:00:19.351 --> 00:00:22.021
Then I found out we were
gonna do "Amber Says What"

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:24.824
from home,
and I was like, "What?!"

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:28.094
But then, I found out
that no one was gonna dress me,

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:30.530
and they were like,
"Dress yourself,"

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.999
and I was like, "Wh-a-a-at?"

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:36.002
Okay, but you asked for it.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:38.238
I've got evening gowns for days.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:42.441
I've gone to the Emmys
five times. To lose.

00:00:42.441 --> 00:00:45.144
So I might as well wear
something that shows this virus

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:47.012
that I'm too glamorous.

00:00:47.012 --> 00:00:48.247
So, first they were like,

00:00:48.247 --> 00:00:50.549
"Amber, you're gonna
film this on Zoom."

00:00:50.549 --> 00:00:53.219
And I was like,
"What...is Zoom?

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:55.422
Is it that
the children's PBS show

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:57.724
where little kids
run around unsupervised?"

00:00:57.724 --> 00:01:00.960
Because I do not care
for unsupervised children.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.496
And when we found out
that we were gonna have to

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:05.198
shelter in place,
I was like --

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:09.068
♪ What ♪
I am about to thrive!

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:11.771
Now, my husband may be going
a little crazy, because

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:14.874
he's used to physical activity,
but I'm not.

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:17.143
I've been training for this
my whole life.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.978
I call it having a seat.

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:21.781
And if having a seat
was an Olympic sport,

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.816
I would bring home the gold.

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:25.584
Speaking of the Olympics,

00:01:25.584 --> 00:01:28.688
International Olympic Committee
member Dick Pound

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.756
said the Olympics
will be postponed.

00:01:30.756 --> 00:01:33.793
And I was like,
"What...is your name?"

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.561
Dick Pound?!

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:37.096
Are you named after the place

00:01:37.096 --> 00:01:39.399
stray dicks go
when they're caught?

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:41.033
Dick Pound?

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:43.937
Are you named after what
Frankenstein says during sex?

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:45.504
[ Deep voice ] "Dick Pound."

00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:47.706
[ Normal voice] Are you named
after the cheapest gigolo

00:01:47.706 --> 00:01:48.974
in London?

00:01:48.974 --> 00:01:51.777
"Dick? Why, that'll
only be a pound, gov'nah."

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:53.045
Your name is wrong.

00:01:53.045 --> 00:01:55.081
And you know Dick Pound
was like,

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:57.917
"Oh, no, people are gonna
be home with nothing to do.

00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:00.653
Do you think they're finally
gonna notice my name?"

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:03.055
Yeah, Dick, we're gonna.

00:02:03.055 --> 00:02:06.792
And then Trump called the
coronavirus the Chinese virus.

00:02:06.792 --> 00:02:09.495
And I was like,
"What...a racist."

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:10.863
Calling it Chinese

00:02:10.863 --> 00:02:13.132
doesn't absolve of you
of responsibility for it.

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:15.568
That'd be like me
blaming a fart on Seth.

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:17.336
We're not in the same room
right now,

00:02:17.336 --> 00:02:19.906
so I have to accept
I have a hand in it.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:24.277
Then Trump had a phone call
with Chinese leader Xi Jinping.

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.979
Now, did he call it
the Chinese virus then?

00:02:26.979 --> 00:02:29.549
Of course not,
because he was talking directly

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:33.519
to a Chinese person,
and all racists are cowards.

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:37.323
Then a member of the White House
coronavirus task force,

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:40.459
Dr. Anthony Fauci, explained
that he can't stop Trump

00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:43.229
from telling lies at press
conferences because

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:46.399
"I can't jump in front of the
microphone and push him down."

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:48.601
And I was like, "What?"

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:51.871
If you're gonna push anyone
down, it should be Donald Trump.

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:54.173
It'll be easy.
Look at how he stands.

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:57.376
He leans so far over,
he's already half down.

00:02:57.376 --> 00:03:00.479
What...kind of doctor are you?

00:03:00.479 --> 00:03:02.915
You see a man saying things in
public that are harming people

00:03:02.915 --> 00:03:04.317
and you do nothing?

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:06.452
Look, if I get on national TV

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:10.022
and tell everyone to lick their
doorknobs, freaking tackle me.

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:12.825
Then I found out that
"Contagion" and "Outbreak"

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:14.660
are among
the most-streamed films

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:16.896
during the pandemic,
and I was like, "What?"

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:18.831
Why would you
watch those right now?

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:21.534
Just go to your window
and look outside.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:24.703
Those two movies are
live-streaming all around you.

00:03:24.703 --> 00:03:27.941
You're the star, and it's free!

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:30.076
Then I heard a crazy rumor.

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:35.381
I heard Vladimir Putin released
lions onto the streets in Russia

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:38.551 line:0%
to get people to stay at home,
and I was like...

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.486 line:0%
Now, it turns out
that wasn't true,

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:42.621
but I totally believed it
at first.

00:03:42.621 --> 00:03:46.626
Why? Because releasing lions
to keep people indoors

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:49.428
is something a shirtless man
would totally do.

00:03:49.428 --> 00:03:51.930
Now, I learned all about
shirtless men and tigers

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:53.365
by watching "Tiger King."

00:03:53.365 --> 00:03:55.601
And I need you to watch it
because I've got to talk

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:57.570
to everyone I know about it
forever,

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:00.039
because that whole
freaking thing is like, what?

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:02.976
Then I found out
Arnold Schwarzenegger

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:07.079
has been posting self-isolation
videos of him eating meals

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:10.650
at home with his tiny donkey
and miniature horse.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.351
And I saw that
and was like, "What?"

00:04:12.351 --> 00:04:15.855
Are you eating off the same
plate as a freaking donkey?

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:19.625
Do you not know
how all this got started?

00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:23.028
Are we witnessing
the beginning of donkey flu?

00:04:23.028 --> 00:04:24.664
[As Arnold]
"I'll be back...

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:27.166
in 14 days after
self-quarantining

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:29.269
because I got the donkey virus."

00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:31.203
[ Normal voice ]
Then everyone was like,

00:04:31.203 --> 00:04:33.772
"You got to use Zoom
to call your friends

00:04:33.772 --> 00:04:36.175
to make yourself feel better,"
and I was like, "What?!"

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:38.911
I use Zoom to make myself
feel better.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:41.381
All I need is this...

00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:43.549
and this.

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:46.386
Hm. Mostly this.

00:04:46.386 --> 00:04:48.454
This has been "Amber Says What."

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:49.922
♪♪

